h korea's  leader kim jong-un met in the dmz  those talks didn't end the armed  standoff but future ones may well  succeed which could open this pristine  area to development  instead kim tells his students and  anyone else who will listen the best  monument for peace between the korean  peoples  would be a protected home for its  animals  a dmz national park  for cbs morning's elizabeth palmer near  the dmz south korea  so i often wonder  if the world without us what would it be  like for the animals and you get a  little window into that in that two-mile  160 mile long stretch they have a good  time without us don't they you sure  enjoy it yeah i've never seen a water  deer before with vampires ever that kind  of blew my mind

